                <h2>Applicable Scenarios and Inspection Frequency</h2>
<p>This SOP applies to operations teams managing overseas advertising platforms such as Meta (Facebook), Google, TikTok, and Pinterest. Routine inspections are recommended once per week; if there are abnormal operations, significant budget adjustments, or platform policy updates, inspections should be increased to daily.</p>
<blockquote>
<p><strong>Note</strong>: Inspection is not only a risk control measure but also the foundation for optimizing delivery efficiency. It is recommended to embed inspections into the team's daily workflow rather than waiting for problems to occur.</p>
</blockquote>
<hr />
<h2>Step 1: Account Status Inspection</h2>
<ol>
<li>Log into the ad dashboard and check for any warning alerts or restriction notices</li>
<li>Verify account permissions to ensure only active employees have management access</li>
<li>Confirm that linked payment methods (credit card/payment account) are in normal status</li>
<li>Ensure BM (Business Manager) asset ownership is clear to avoid cross-account confusion</li>
</ol>
<p><strong>Exception Handling</strong>: If the account is restricted or a policy warning is received, take screenshots immediately and contact platform support or agency channel within 24 hours to submit an appeal.</p>
<hr />
<h2>Step 2: Payment and Recharge Reconciliation</h2>
<ol>
<li>Log into the agency or official backend to verify account balance matches recharge records</li>
<li>Review recent billing statements for any unauthorized charges or abnormal deductions</li>
<li>Confirm recharge arrival time meets platform promises (usually within 1-24 hours)</li>
<li>Ensure account budget settings match actual delivery needs to avoid overspending</li>
</ol>
<p><strong>Risk Point</strong>: Some agency channels may experience recharge delays or funds not arriving. Always verify balance changes after recharging.</p>
<hr />
<h2>Step 3: Ad Creative Compliance Review</h2>
<ol>
<li>Verify all live creatives comply with platform community guidelines and advertising policies</li>
<li>Key review items:</li>
<li>Landing page links are accessible and consistent with ad claims</li>
<li>Images/videos contain no misleading content, exaggerated claims, or prohibited elements</li>
<li>Copy does not include absolute terms or unverified efficacy statements</li>
<li>Confirm creatives have passed platform review or have no pending review status</li>
</ol>
<p><strong>Quick Checklist</strong>:<br />
- [ ] All landing pages load normally<br />
- [ ] No political, religious, or violent content<br />
- [ ] No false discounts or price misleading<br />
- [ ] Copyright music/material usage is compliant</p>
<hr />
<h2>Step 4: Targeting Parameters Review</h2>
<ol>
<li>Verify targeting settings contain no discriminatory delivery or prohibited audience exclusions</li>
<li>Check ad group/campaign naming is standardized for easy data attribution</li>
<li>Confirm bidding strategies and budget allocation match expectations with no abnormal bid fluctuations</li>
<li>Review scheduling and frequency controls are reasonable to avoid overexposure</li>
</ol>
<hr />
<h2>Step 5: Data and Financial Reconciliation</h2>
<ol>
<li>Export current period spend reports and reconcile with agency or platform bills</li>
<li>Check for abnormally high or low spend ad groups and identify causes</li>
<li>Verify core metrics like ROI/CAC for significant abnormal fluctuations</li>
<li>Maintain complete reconciliation records for audit and financial traceability</li>
</ol>
<p><strong>Recommended Tool</strong>: Use Yiyu Digital Media's multi-account management dashboard to view all account balances, spend, and recharge status in one click, improving reconciliation efficiency.</p>
<hr />
<h2>Inspection Records and Reporting</h2>
<p>After completing the above five steps, fill out the inspection record form with:<br />
- Inspection date and person responsible<br />
- Check results for each module (normal/abnormal)<br />
- Abnormal items discovered and handling status<br />
- Follow-up items for next inspection</p>
<p><strong>Reporting Mechanism</strong>: If major anomalies are found (such as impending account suspension or significant financial discrepancies), immediately report to the team leader and initiate emergency procedures.</p>
<hr />
<h2>Appendix: Common Compliance Issues Quick Reference</h2>
<table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Issue Type</th>
<th>Typical Symptoms</th>
<th>Recommended Actions</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>Account Restricted</td>
<td>Cannot deliver, received platform email</td>
<td>Appeal immediately, prepare credentials</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Recharge Not Received</td>
<td>Backend balance not updated</td>
<td>Contact agency/platform customer service</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Creative Rejected</td>
<td>Ad review failed</td>
<td>Modify creative or submit appeal</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Abnormal Spend</td>
<td>Sudden increase or stoppage</td>
<td>Check ad status and bidding settings</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Payment Failed</td>
<td>Credit card declined or insufficient balance</td>
<td>Update payment method or recharge</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<hr />
<p>Following this SOP for routine inspections can effectively reduce compliance risks in overseas advertising and ensure stable account operations. Contact the Yiyu Digital Media team for more risk control strategies or account management tips.</p>
